# Relations this migration declares; probed by db-schema/tests/schema_fence.rs.
#
# One nullable ADD COLUMN against a table 0011 created, plus a `COMMENT ON
# COLUMN`. Neither is a relation, so the existence probe is blind to it — the
# same position 0014_fair_price_leg_staleness is in.
#
# The column is asserted by its writer and reader instead:
# `fx_tape_live_follows_the_fx_leg_contributors` and
# `a_degraded_composition_reads_back_through_the_reader` in
# market-data/tests/fair_price_roundtrip.rs. Like 0014's, those tests are
# `#[ignore]`d and operator-run rather than a merge gate.
none alters a table 0011 created — adds one nullable column and its comment, not a relation
